<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Build tools are here<br><br>See <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/Voice_Prompts/tools" class="postlink">downloads/Voice_Prompts/tools</a></div></blockquote>I guess these tools are to create new voices?<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Localisation text files are here, but won't be the latest for the last beta, you will need to use the beta localisation files<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/localisation/voice_prompt_texts" class="postlink">downloads/localisation/voice_prompt_texts</a></div></blockquote>ok, I've checked this ones: <a href="https://drive.proton.me/urls/256SP2W1NM#mC9d2L32MEmb" class="postlink">https://drive.proton.me/urls/256SP2W1NM#mC9d2L32MEmb</a> from the last beta: <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=19&amp;t=4815" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=19&amp;t=4815</a><br><br>but what I want to know is if there is a way to test the XML files in the current voices to know is they sound properly? for example to verify pronunciations and some separated/individual characters modulation.</div></blockquote>We use a free online service called <a href="https://ttsmp3.com/" class="postlink">https://ttsmp3.com/</a>  to generate the voice files.<br><br>That site lets you type in text and listen to the audio.<br><br>However, be aware becuase ita a free service it has a limited number of words it will generate per day<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Feb 06, 2025 4:48 am</p><hr />
